# Automated Lead Intake & Follow-Up System

**Tools used:** n8n, Baserow, Google Sheets/Forms, Gmail, Abstract API

## The Problem

Manually tracking new contacts/leads is easy to fall behind on — entries pile up in a spreadsheet or inbox, get lost, and follow-ups slip through the cracks. There's no automatic way to know when someone new comes in, whether their contact info is even valid, or when it's time to follow up.

## What I Built

A two-part automation system that turns a simple form into a self-maintaining mini-CRM:

**1. Intake Pipeline** — triggers the moment a new contact is submitted:
- Captures new submissions from a Google Form via a Google Sheets trigger
- Validates and enriches the email address using the Abstract API (deliverability status, MX records, sender/organization data)
- Writes the enriched record into a Baserow CRM table
- Sends a real-time email notification with the new contact's details

**2. Follow-Up Scheduler** — runs independently on a daily timer:
- Queries the CRM for contacts still marked "New"
- Filters for entries older than 3 days with no status update
- Sends a reminder email listing exactly who still needs follow-up

